WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
Zero Trust depends on visibility because access decisions are only as informed as the

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.020
available signals.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.900
Organizations need useful information about identities, devices, applications, data,

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.900
networks, policy actions, and security events.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.040
Monitoring begins before access with authentication, device, resource, and risk context.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.930
It continues during and after access through session events, application logs,

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.360
policy decisions, administrative activity, and changes in security posture.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.738
Continuous evaluation allows policy to respond when conditions change.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:33.360
A request that was acceptable earlier may deserve additional verification or reduced

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.040
access if risk increases,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.480
the device becomes noncompliant, or activity no longer matches expected use.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.260
Policy decisions should be observable.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.210
Logging which policy was evaluated, which signals were available,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.125
and why access was allowed, limited,

00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:50.960
or denied helps operations teams troubleshoot problems and review security outcomes.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.150
Data quality matters.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.560
Missing logs, inconsistent identity fields, unsynchronized timestamps,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.960
unclear asset ownership, and short retention can weaken analysis.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.180
Visibility programs should measure coverage and document known limitations.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.490
Analytics can help identify patterns and prioritize review,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:09.795
but automated risk scores should not become unexplained authority.

00:01:09.795 --> 00:01:12.535
Organizations need governance, testing, thresholds, human oversight,

00:01:12.535 --> 00:01:14.990
and a way to correct inaccurate decisions.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.000
Monitoring supports response and improvement.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.330
Security teams can investigate unusual access, identify policy gaps, tune controls,

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:25.790
assist affected users, and feed lessons into identity, endpoint, application,

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.004
and network programs.

00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:29.900
Visibility must be balanced with privacy and legal requirements.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.350
Collection should have a defined security purpose, appropriate access control,

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.960
retention limits, protection, and transparent governance.
